That's super strange! I'd be very surprised if the format of the classfiles changes between JDK updates - I wonder what causes the problem.

There's no reason you can't compile Renjin with an earlier of update of Java 7. We could also build Renjin releases with an earlier version of Java 7, but I'd be curious to know what exactly this would change at the compilation stage (I would have expected most changes to be at runtime).

